  "worked_solution": "First, we convert from quarts to gallons. There are $4$ quarts in each gallon, so we divide the number of quarts by $4:$     \n\n$$\n20÷4=5\n$$\n\nSo, $20$ quarts is the same as $5$ gallons. Now, to find the unit price per gallon, we divide the total price by $5:$ \n\n$$\n16.80÷5=3.36\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gasoline costs $$3.36$ per gallon.",
